# Project 1 – Deploy a 3-Tier Web Application on EKS

## Architecture Overview

A common enterprise application has three layers:

1. Frontend
2. Backend API
3. Database

Architecture:

```text id="w3x8c2"
                    Users

                      |

              Application Load Balancer

                      |

                  Frontend Pods

                      |

                  API Service

                      |

                  Backend Pods

                      |

                 Database Layer

                      |

              Amazon RDS / Storage
```

---

# 1. Components Used

## Frontend

Technology examples:

* React
* Angular
* Nginx

Runs as:

```text id="r8k4m1"
Frontend Deployment

        |

        |

Frontend Pods
```

---

## Backend

Examples:

* Java Spring Boot
* Node.js
* Python Flask

Runs as:

```text id="t5n8q2"
Backend Deployment

        |

        |

API Pods
```

---

## Database

Production recommendation:

Use managed database:

* Amazon RDS
* Amazon Aurora

Instead of running databases inside Kubernetes.

---

# 2. Project Architecture

```text id="f2m7k9"

                    Internet

                       |

                  Route 53

                       |

                     ALB

                       |

                 Kubernetes Ingress

                       |

        --------------------------------

        Frontend Service

              |

        Frontend Pods


        Backend Service

              |

        Backend Pods


        --------------------------------

                    |

                  RDS

```

---

# 3. Kubernetes Resources Required

Application requires:

```text id="c9m2x5"

Namespace

|

Deployments

|

Services

|

ConfigMaps

|

Secrets

|

Ingress

|

Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
```

---

# 4. Create Namespace

Example:

```bash
kubectl create namespace ecommerce
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get namespaces
```

---

# 5. Frontend Deployment

Example:

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1

kind: Deployment

metadata:

 name: frontend


spec:

 replicas: 3


 selector:

  matchLabels:

   app: frontend


 template:

  metadata:

   labels:

    app: frontend


  spec:

   containers:

   - name: frontend

     image: nginx
```

---

# 6. Frontend Service

```yaml
apiVersion: v1

kind: Service

metadata:

 name: frontend-service


spec:

 selector:

  app: frontend


 ports:

 - port: 80

   targetPort: 80
```

---

# 7. Backend Deployment

Architecture:

```text id="p6s8w1"
Backend Deployment

        |

        |

Backend Pods

        |

        |

API Service
```

Example:

```yaml
kind: Deployment

metadata:

 name: backend


spec:

 replicas: 3
```

---

# 8. Configuration Management

Applications need configuration.

Example:

Database URL:

```text id="n7q2x4"
DATABASE_HOST=rds.example.com
```

Use ConfigMap:

```bash
kubectl create configmap app-config
```

---

# 9. Secrets

Sensitive information:

* Passwords
* API keys
* Tokens

Use:

* Kubernetes Secrets
* AWS Secrets Manager

Example:

```text id="k8m3z6"
Application

      |

Secret

      |

Database Password
```

---

# 10. Ingress Configuration

Traffic flow:

```text id="v4m9k1"

User

 |

ALB

 |

Ingress

 |

Service

 |

Pod
```

Example:

```yaml
kind: Ingress

metadata:

 name: app-ingress
```

---

# 11. Application Scaling

Use Horizontal Pod Autoscaler.

Example:

```text id="q2w8m7"
Low Traffic

3 Pods


High Traffic

10 Pods
```

Command:

```bash
kubectl autoscale deployment frontend \
--min=3 \
--max=10 \
--cpu-percent=70
```

